  "notes": [
    "Sony's official Japanese SCPH-10010 instruction manual (3-059-053-03 (1)), PDF page 2, fetched and visually checked on 2026-11-01. Its labelled analog-mode front/top diagrams provide the complete control list: one directional pad, four shape buttons, two sticks (L3/R3 are their clicks), L1/R1, L2/R2, SELECT, START and ANALOG. Archetype vocabulary maps L1/R1 to bumper 2 and the rear L2/R2 row to trigger 2; this names the row, not an analog-travel claim. SELECT/START/ANALOG are button 3. The cable and console-connector diagram establish a permanently attached cable (ports cable 1, wired true). Compatibility includes PlayStation 2, PS one and PlayStation; host_console is the launch PS2 key rather than an exclusive-compatibility claim. The manual publishes no dimensions, mass or cable length, so those remain null. Japanese text was extracted with PDFKit because pypdf garbles its legacy embedded-font mapping; quotes were checked against that extraction and the rendered page."
  ],
